{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/47015-recruitment-orpheus-mission-case-file-0785","id":47015,"title":"[Recruitment][Orpheus] Mission Case File #0785","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-11T12:57:41-08:00","id":47015,"title":"[Recruitment][Orpheus] Mission Case File #0785","content":"<i>Elisa Chambers let out sigh as she sifted through reports on her desk, searching in vain hope for an answer to her problems. But there was nothing, nothing but more disappointment and frustration. How had things gone so pear-shaped in a single night? The job had been a simple investigation and possible fumigation of a noisy but non-violent PLE from an abandoned asylum so the site could be renovated. Now she had a ghost and two sleepers MIA, one skimmer KIA and other deeply traumatized with no solid answers as to what happened.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Compounding the problem there was no other experienced crucibles available to address the situation and this couldn\u2019t wait, not with their agents on the line. But it would look bad for the company if she suddenly called off a crucible in the middle of a mission leaving her with only several inexperienced crucibles, ill suited for a dangerous mission like this.</i><br /> <br /> <i>But what other choice did she have?</i><br /> <br /> <i>Defeated, the middle aged woman leaned back in her chair, rubbing the exhaustion from her eyes. It was her only option. If she waited for another crucible it would look bad. To their agents it would look like middle-management doesn\u2019t care about the people in the field risking their lives, breaking the trust between employee and employer. On the other hand if she pulled another crucible from their current mission to handle this situation their clientele may not understand and in the eyes of management bad PR is worse than the death of agents in the field.</i><br /> <i>In the morning she had a new crucible fresh from training coming in for their first mission, another simple task but one that could wait. This situation took precedence and they could handle it at a later date.</i><br /> <br /> <i>If they survived\u2026</i><br /> <br /> Welcome to my Orpheus Post by Post Chronicle. First time I\u2019ve done a PbP before so we\u2019ll see how it goes. With any luck it will work out well and might even serve off the jumping off point for future chronicles across the Orpheus metaplot (fingers crossed). But first things first\u2026<br /> <br /> Character Creation:<br /> We\u2019re going be using the normal Orpheus character creation process as presented in the Rulebook, though given the nature of PbP RPGs this isn\u2019t really going to be all that heavy on stats and mechanics. Rather this will be so that we all have an idea on what the PCs can do and what they can\u2019t. After all I don\u2019t want to see a PC with no dots in Computers suddenly able to hack into a protected network.<br /> <br /> Laments-all four are available for selection but I am putting a limit on the ghost laments, no more than two. And it\u2019s first come, first serve. Also with ghosts they cannot have died before September 1999, after the Sixth Great Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> Shades-only the default five from the Rulebook are available for this particular game, Banshees, Haunters, Poltergeists, Skinriders and Wisps.<br /> <br /> The Flaws and Merits featured in the second book, Crusade of Ashes can be used as well as the Artifact creation section if you take that background.<br /> <br /> And be sure to include a description of the character as well as a biography. It doesn\u2019t have to be all that long but it should include their near-death experience or death. Oh and if you wish to submit character pictures, whether photo or illustration, that\u2019s fine too.<br /> <br /> Once you have your PC created send to me via PM so I can look it over first. Once I approve it I\u2019ll put your name on the list and you can publicly post them here.<br /> <br /> Oh and be sure to remove any dirty little secrets or other things that other PCs shouldn\u2019t immediately know. I\u2019ve had games in the past where PCs have been biased against other PCs because the players know things their PCs don\u2019t so I like to avoid that as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Due date for submissions: Jan 25<sup>th</sup> or until all slots are full.<br /> <br /> Player Slots:<br /> Minimum of three players, six maximum. And again, first come, first serve.<br /> 1:Jamal Wright [Demdemeh]<br /> 2:<br /> 3:<br /> 4:<br /> 5:<br /> 6:<br /> <br /> <i>Welcome to Orpheus. Hope you survive the experience.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","user":"AkatsukiLeader13","date":". 01-12-2014, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T18:21:23-08:00","id":47771,"title":"","content":"<b>Jamal Wright</b><br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b><br /> Jamal Wright\u2019s eyes glare with nearly single-minded intensity at the subject of his attention, lit by an inner fire. He speaks and moves with precision, barring moments of intense emotion. He may not dominate a room when he enters, but he looms over most other people, standing at a respectable height of 6\u20195\u201d, built like a linebacker. Despite his size, he moves with care and grace. <br /> <br /> <b>History:</b><br /> Jamal grew up in the inner city with his mother and father. He worked hard and, for the most part, avoided trouble. Eventually, he earned a football scholarship to a good university where he studied pre-law. He was especially fascinated by pigment, and its potential ties to Orpheus, but his investigation turned into recruitment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1768-demdemeh","name":"Demdemeh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}